    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** serving as our clear offensive anchor, boasting an elite 82.37 score. His placement in the #2 spot against the vulnerable xERA of Elder, combined with a dynamic platoon advantage, makes him the premier start to generate the stolen bases we desperately need to climb the standings. Following close behind in the \"Strong\" tier is **Max Muncy**, who benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost against Bradford. Despite hitting 7th, **Max Muncy**\u2019s park factors and BvP track record inflate his score to 68.95, making him a high-efficiency play. Similarly, **Henry Bolte** is locked in as a top-tier option (65.40); his move to the leadoff spot against Bradford, paired with favorable wind conditions and a significant platoon edge, provides the perfect setup for run production at the top of the order.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was undoubtedly **Jose Caballero**. He finished at 39.32, landing just below our 40.0 floor. While we weigh stolen base threats heavily, the combination of facing an elite arm in Cease and an unfavorable platoon split ultimately pushed him out of the starting nine. We continue to monitor the status of **James Wood**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Vinnie Pasquantino**, who remain sidelined on the IL, leaving our active depth limited. Meanwhile, we remain wary of **Zach McKinstry**; his score of 40.43 is perilously close to the bench threshold, largely due to a tough matchup against the 3.38 xERA of Burke. We will monitor the real-time weather and any late-breaking lineup changes for **Gabriel Moreno** and **Austin Riley**, as their mid-to-low range scores leave them vulnerable if defensive replacements or late adjustments occur. We have confidence that our current alignment maximizes our exposure to the weakest opposing arms available today.",
